{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3401761316b9a45318d1445a3ed4e155a1aaf428ae431b97b4db090a87603af6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Interactive no-argument cli/app launches show a numbered picker where Enter prefers the workspace-bound profile, exact names take precedence over menu numbers, and scripts must pass an explicit profile name."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6cc76ea236a81e7f87a9c7b02224983ae390c13acb0fe94cc105f26ff30a41b8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is described as a single Bash script with no runtime dependencies beyond standard system tools; it requires Bash and a working upstream Codex CLI, and does not install Codex itself."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3401761316b9a45318d1445a3ed4e155a1aaf428ae431b97b4db090a87603af6","clm_6cc76ea236a81e7f87a9c7b02224983ae390c13acb0fe94cc105f26ff30a41b8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_1b92011feed1458480a21273bb99f24f","id":"pg_60046a00693252d982ed150f3ab08155","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/ducksss-codex-profiles-agent-md-5a8084bf8a3a-150f3ab08155.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6365f3b5c1c45e259ec87b9726584724"],"title":"Ducksss/codex-profiles/agent.md @ 5a8084bf8a3a","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:01Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1b92011feed1458480a21273bb99f24f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0f0a755eeb5c2d671f665b20821b2f7e79f5893373d55de6ae4a30ec4efca252"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"shell-init prints shell code for bash/zsh/fish that enables 'use <profile>' in the current shell, with optional --prompt and --completions; it never edits shell startup files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d3d37944a9a4dad2d2ca9f3a88528ce45f18beff46a40e384be9a2e376b6f28"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project states local-state separation is not an account, OS, or server-side security boundary; OS credentials, network, keychain, and other tool credentials remain shared or outside its control."},{"claim_ids":["clm_47b39d0ba69be4f8423713ecdc48992e04c1bd68d5e3534109889f194ca1d7a9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool does not verify that CLI and Desktop sign-ins use the same account, and does not change or inspect server-side ChatGPT workspaces, policies, histories, or plans."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5cae3c65513751e7ecb2aac094d699c95a7da37e5cc5227c18ced9c46871fa06"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project recommends itself for people using multiple Codex contexts who want separate Codex homes or named ChatGPT windows with separate local state on macOS, without copying authentication files."},{"claim_ids":["clm_736af6f8f0fbb86328234119a715ed4f034224e12a0b2bf18630d677d641fee9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A workspace guard defaults to warn mode; strict mode rejects mismatched cli, env/use, and app selections before side effects, and off disables checks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8280cb2416789a2dcb3962829abfd0f3c4c68e7cdb5a009e79afd8b4fcb28712"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"launcher create builds a small unsigned macOS app in ~/Applications (overridable via CODEX_PROFILE_LAUNCHER_ROOT) that calls codex-profile app <profile>, with named/color-coded identities and list/path/remove subcommands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_927d02ad5a8e4edc5170e94819acfe5bc9dcdfaa5923881bd104e9b9c758cde6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Profile selection maps the name 'default' to ~/.codex and any other name <x> to ~/.codex-<x>, so each profile gets its own Codex home."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c9215aa4dc531c6a0aac96aae0e6fa696f64252bf080a8f03be13cd9e28e7f89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workspace bindings store only a canonical path and profile name under ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/codex-profile with private permissions, relocatable via CODEX_PROFILE_CONFIG_HOME; nested bindings override ancestors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d460a1787f8ec9bce381627583d0067c1b41d34802ca86000983d00433f23bc7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool exposes a CLI with commands including setup, init, login, cli, app, run, list, status, doctor, path, shell-init, workspace bind, launcher create, env, and detach."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e749ca8a51eaee584b966fb2e9fc4824c812e2702e70ca39e2a2f5fa0a58c146"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"init --share-with links only a fixed allowlist of configuration entries (config.toml, AGENTS.md, instructions.md, rules/, plugins/, etc.) while auth.json, sessions, and Electron data stay per-profile; the tool never reads or copies authentication tokens or cookies."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0f0a755eeb5c2d671f665b20821b2f7e79f5893373d55de6ae4a30ec4efca252","clm_1d3d37944a9a4dad2d2ca9f3a88528ce45f18beff46a40e384be9a2e376b6f28","clm_47b39d0ba69be4f8423713ecdc48992e04c1bd68d5e3534109889f194ca1d7a9","clm_5cae3c65513751e7ecb2aac094d699c95a7da37e5cc5227c18ced9c46871fa06","clm_736af6f8f0fbb86328234119a715ed4f034224e12a0b2bf18630d677d641fee9","clm_8280cb2416789a2dcb3962829abfd0f3c4c68e7cdb5a009e79afd8b4fcb28712","clm_927d02ad5a8e4edc5170e94819acfe5bc9dcdfaa5923881bd104e9b9c758cde6","clm_c9215aa4dc531c6a0aac96aae0e6fa696f64252bf080a8f03be13cd9e28e7f89","clm_d460a1787f8ec9bce381627583d0067c1b41d34802ca86000983d00433f23bc7","clm_e749ca8a51eaee584b966fb2e9fc4824c812e2702e70ca39e2a2f5fa0a58c146"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:01Z","created_by_operation":"op_1b92011feed1458480a21273bb99f24f","id":"pg_be55e5c66bbf